# DesignCheck — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to a new file named `.env.local` in the same folder, fill
# in real values, then restart `npm run dev` (or redeploy on Vercel).
# `.env.local` is already git-ignored — never commit real keys.
#
# You do NOT need any of these to try the app — click "Try Demo" on the
# home page to see a full example with no setup at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) Figma sign-in ("Connect Figma") — required for real (non-demo)
#    analysis. This is an OAuth app, NOT a personal access token: every
#    designer who uses your deployed DesignCheck signs in with their OWN
#    Figma account and only ever grants access to their own files. You are
#    just registering the *app* once, not sharing your own Figma access.
#
#    How to get these (free, 5 minutes):
#    1. Go to https://www.figma.com/developers/apps and log in.
#    2. Click "Create a new app".
#    3. App name: anything, e.g. "DesignCheck". Website URL: anything,
#       e.g. your GitHub repo or http://localhost:3000 for now.
#    4. Under "Callback URL" / "Redirect URIs", add:
#         http://localhost:3000/api/auth/figma/callback
#       (for testing on your own computer). Once you deploy to Vercel
#       (see the README's deployment section), come back and ALSO add
#       your live URL the same way, e.g.:
#         https://your-app-name.vercel.app/api/auth/figma/callback
#       If the form only allows one URL at a time, add one now and the
#       other after you have your Vercel URL — you can edit this later.
#    5. Save the app. Figma shows you a "Client ID" and a "Client Secret" —
#       copy both below. The secret is only shown once; if you lose it,
#       generate a new one from the same app settings page.
FIGMA_CLIENT_ID=
FIGMA_CLIENT_SECRET=

# 2) Session secret — used only to encrypt each designer's sign-in cookie
#    in their own browser (not shared, not a Figma value). Any long random
#    string works. Easiest way to generate one:
#    - In your terminal, inside this project folder, run:
#        node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#    - Copy the long string it prints and paste it below.
SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) Google Gemini API key — OPTIONAL. Used only to generate a friendlier,
#    one-sentence "why this matters" explanation for each issue. Every
#    measurement (colors, spacing, text, sizes) works perfectly without
#    this — it's a nice-to-have, not a requirement.
#
#    How to get one (free, no credit card):
#    1. Go to https://aistudio.google.com
#    2. Click "Get API key" → "Create API key".
#    3. Copy the key and paste it below.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override which Gemini model is used (defaults to a fast,
# low-cost model). Check https://ai.google.dev/models if this is retired.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
